SUMMARY:Outdoor Gallery: Art to merch panel discussion as part of Outdoor G
 allery ‘AMPLIFY ME!’
DESCRIPTION:Step into a workshop buzzing with ideas and the potential to tr
 ansform your artwork into merchandise. Drawing on the diverse practices of
  the AMPLIFY ME! Outdoor Gallery artists\, this engaging session explores 
 creative pathways from concept to product. Hear real-world examples\, prac
 tical tips and personal stories from artists who are building sustainable 
 creative careers through their work. Expect a lively\, collaborative envir
 onment where connections are made\, ideas are sparked and the seeds of you
 r own creative future begin to take shape. This program is part of Council
 ’s latest Outdoor Gallery exhibition\, AMPLIFY ME! \, a celebration of l
 ocal Brisbane artists with lived experience of disability that showcases t
 heir work in accessible outdoor spaces across the city. Grounded in inclus
 ive arts practice\, the exhibition encourages collaboration and barrier-fr
 ee creativity\, supporting lasting connections\, inclusion and social chan
 ge across Brisbane’s cultural landscape. AMPLIFY ME! is curated by Nicol
 e Crosswell and runs from 21 November 2025 to 25 October 2026. Council’s
  Outdoor Gallery transforms Brisbane’s laneways\, streets and car parks 
 into imaginative spaces for everyone\, showcasing art in light boxes\, ban
 ners\, vitrines and evening projections. Image Credit: Ruby Herrenberg wit
 h Amplify Me! Amplify You!! 2025 Artist Collaboration located in Edward St
 reet. Photography by Joseph Rucklie.
LOCATION:Suburban Business Hub\, Nundah\, Suburban Business Hub\, 16 Aspina
 ll Street\, Nundah
